    {
      "paths": [
        "src/EnemyManager.cpp",
        "src/EnemyManager.hpp"
      ],
      "change": "g_SpellcardScore u32 -> i32; target signed FILD DWORD in ECL; full 30156-byte procedure including switch tables replays exactly."
    },
    {
      "paths": [
        "src/EnemyManager.cpp",
        "src/EnemyManager.hpp"
      ],
      "change": "Move Initialize definition out of the class; preserve its body and original call boundary, removing unused VC7 inline-reservation slots in constructor and RegisterChain."
    },
    {
      "paths": [
        "src/main.cpp"
      ],
      "change": "Express the observed DWORD-aligned QueryPerformanceCounter sample as its two 32-bit fields; retain the 8-byte x86 API buffer layout."
    },
    {
      "paths": [
        "src/BulletManager.cpp"
      ],
      "change": "Compare template index against unsigned ARRAY_SIZE, matching the original JAE rather than JGE."
    },
    {
      "paths": [
        "src/Ending.cpp"
      ],
      "change": "Use atoi and 32-bit int result; independently identify the original 5-byte CRT forwarding entry by complete tail-thunk replay."
    },
    {
      "paths": [
        "src/MainMenu.cpp",
        "src/MainMenuPreInput.cpp",
        "src/AnmManager.hpp"
      ],
      "change": "Move OnUpdatePreInput into a native COFF TU with the observed constructor call preserved by a TU-local noinline declaration hint. Constructor body/layout/ABI remain shared. Use size-profile diagnostic stubs, /Od /Oi headers and the menu size/ordinary-strcpy profile. Complete 3184-byte routine, including 32 table bytes, replays in the maintained linked product."
    },
    {
      "paths": [
        "src/ResultScreen.hpp",
        "src/ResultScreen.cpp",
        "src/ResultRegister.cpp",
        "src/ResultScreenCtor.cpp"
      ],
      "change": "Initialize the POD score-node grid explicitly through one shared stride/count loop. A TU-local noinline hint removes its speculative argument homes in native registration; a native dllexport constructor emitter preserves the exact shared 251-byte constructor. Class/initializer bodies and layout do not vary by TU. This emits one additional constructor export; full PE identity is not claimed. Complete 339/251/265-byte registration/constructor/deletion and all 694 named routines replay exactly with independently proven complete EH capsule aliases."
    },
